GET /api/companies/{company_id}/alerts/low-stock

Assumptions

Recent sales = sales in last 30 days

Threshold varies by product type

One primary supplier per product

Stockout days calculated using average daily sales

@GetMapping("/api/companies/{companyId}/alerts/low-stock")
public ResponseEntity<?> getLowStockAlerts(@PathVariable Long companyId) {

    List<LowStockAlertDTO> alerts = inventoryService.getLowStockAlerts(companyId);

    return ResponseEntity.ok(
        Map.of(
            "alerts", alerts,
            "total_alerts", alerts.size()
        )
    );
}

for each warehouse in company:
    for each product with recent sales:
        if current_stock < threshold:
            calculate days_until_stockout
            fetch supplier
            add alert


edge Cases Handled

No recent sales → no alert

Zero stock → immediate alert

Missing supplier → partial alert

Multiple warehouses → separate alerts

*****Why This Works

Business-driven filtering

Scalable for large inventories

Clear separation of concerns

Easy to extend for notifications
